{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-123892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the area bounded by graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-123892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35