d ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123889" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-123889" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123889" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2+\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123889" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/7a48288304608aa9d2b68a34794183cf58308ce16487c1675318180936868674.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4},$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\pi $ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}(\\theta {|}_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ){|}_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}((\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-(\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25\\pi }{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{25\\pi }{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{25\\pi }{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-123894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25\\pi }{16}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}-\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{9}{8}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-352284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{9}{8}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{8}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +18}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-352303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}+\\frac{9}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(16+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(16+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta -16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\,) \\\\  & =9\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =3\\pi -8(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-352323" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352323" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\pi-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/4f3086c30f3c442e19e0844311b9ee57a75a517496861380a8bf3836c5adb539.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\pi $ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(25+20\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(25+20\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(27\\theta -20\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(27\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-20\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}(2\\pi -\\pi )-10(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{2}-10(1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{2}-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-352319" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6