" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-14866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-9643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area bounded by the polar curve $r=3{e}^{2\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-9643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3{e}^{2\\theta }$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{(3{e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4\\theta }\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}({e}^{4\\pi }-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}({e}^{4\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324