uestion/worked-solution" "value" "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2{e}^{1-\\theta }$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(2{e}^{1-\\theta })^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}4{e}^{2-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{e}^{-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{-2\\theta }}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}(\\frac{1}{9}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a6a6f2e0d52cdc97bad9994464a9e36db8c8db3d9955c7739a2d37a3ce7112c"} {"question" "q-352338" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/state.json" "file_sha256" "519a019823874153172bda6d3b0e5f0f9ee7d35bc4f2ed4207a850b29324d2e1"} {"question" "q-352338" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8e^2}{9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/q